    "findings": [
      "Dynamic and QoS flags require GPU live counter and fresh voltage-floor handshake; unavailable before GPU activation is expected, not proof of a fault.",
      "SwEmcNotReady -6 can mean CPU, core or GPU floor provider not ready; telemetry alone does not identify which one.",
      "ACTMON -1 can mean missing interrupt/maps or invalid initialization parameters; retain as failure, not a pending GPU handshake.",
      "Before activation accept -6 only with working ACTMON, fresh enumerated rate, unchanged high boot rate, no transitions, no dynamic/QoS flags and no fault flags. After activation require all error fields zero and full dynamic/QoS readiness."
    ],
    "limits": [
      "Source alone is not native proof; the original-baseline closed-start observation now independently verifies the pending-state pattern.",
      "No FAN or KMD code changed."
    ],
